# Implement explicit import and export

## Scope and existing evidence

Allow deliberate notebook bundle and `.atrament` profile reads or writes at
caller-selected or explicitly host-policy-admitted paths without converting them
into background persistence. Keep paths mentioned only in notebook, source,
diagnostic, clipboard, or model-response text as data rather than Export
authority.

Current export design evidence freezes accepted-revision binding, caller-owned
or
explicit host-policy output intent, explicit path and overwrite behavior,
blocking validation, temporary cleanup, file-commit semantics, output identity,
same-retry lost-receipt recovery, external target drift handling, cancellation,
typed output results, concurrency, and browser/CLI/MCP parity. File adapters and
format-specific execution remain open. Execution is also blocked on a typed
exportable-artifact payload: current backend code has semantic layout preflight
but no renderer or serializer result value whose admitted bytes a file adapter
can commit. Filesystem writes must not guess that missing artifact-ownership
boundary.

The shared derived/output result domain now freezes all 11 first-release core
result classes and their operation applicability across Render, Plan, and
Export.
It remains vocabulary only: no output operation, receipt normalization, retry
recovery, path handling, or file effect is implemented by that domain.

Its effect disposition separately distinguishes current-call read-only
projection, current-call file commit, recovered prior file commit, and known no
new effect without claiming any receipt or retry-store implementation.

A combined operation/result helper now exposes that disposition only for an
applicable Render, Plan, or Export pair, so callers cannot skip applicability
validation and accidentally project an operation-incompatible result.


Already-qualified lifecycle cancellation can now project into those same output
results without guessing execution state: proven pre-boundary cancellation maps
to Cancelled before result or effect; a crossed Render/Plan completion remains
Completed projection; and a crossed Export file commit remains Exported. A
request alone produces no final result. Cancellation signaling, adapter
execution, receipt normalization, and retry storage remain open.

## Explicit path-intent classification evidence

A transport-neutral `atrament_explicit_file_path_intent` domain now
classifies notebook and handwriting-profile imports and exports before any
file effect. It distinguishes caller selection and independently admitted
host policy from untrusted notebook/source, model, clipboard, and diagnostic
text; all content-derived sources are rejected as path intent.

The contract also rejects missing file-name components, disallows overwrite
requests for Import, preserves opaque non-UTF-8 selected paths, and retains
an explicit preserve-or-replace choice for Export. Integration fixtures cover
all 48 source/purpose/overwrite combinations plus invalid and opaque paths.

The classification is not a filesystem capability and does not check the
truthfulness of its claimed source. The future trusted caller or host adapter
must establish that source independently before invoking this contract and
still enforce path policy, symlink safety, serializer provenance, export
preflight, atomic commits, retry identity, and cancellation. No file has
been imported or exported by this work; the task remains open.

Autonomous Export intent now composes that source-classified path with the
existing autonomous goal-source gate. A 24-case fixture proves that model
text cannot authorize Export even if an independent path is selected, and
that an Import-class path cannot be substituted for an Export target. This
combination is still read-only and does not authorize a file effect.

## Read-only composite Export prerequisite evidence

An `atrament_export_prerequisite_projection` application now combines the
existing independent autonomous Export-source gate, exact Import-versus-Export
selected-path purpose, and revision-bound layout preflight. Its outcomes are
`NoExportIntent`, `WrongPathPurpose`, `BlockedLayout`, `IncompleteLayout`, and
`RequiresArtifactAndFileAdmission`: even the last outcome is **not** complete
Export readiness and cannot authorize a file effect. Source and path selection
remain claims that a future trusted transport must independently verify.

The composition is also reachable through the process-owned
`SessionApplication::preflight_explicit_export_prerequisites` method, which
performs the existing layout-revision binding against current accepted state
before projecting anything. Regression fixtures exercise the 72
source/purpose/layout combinations, genuine empty/incomplete layout evidence,
a genuine 6 mm fixed-region overflow, stale revision rejection after an
accepted semantic edit, and fresh-session refusal. Output artifacts, path
policy, serialization, atomic file commits, retries, and cancellation remain
unimplemented. No persistent output is created by this work.
